  "narrative": "Special Note: ***Calves left untagged are weaned over 45 days*** Compared to last sale (10-08-26): Yearling cattle were too lightly tested to develop any market trend. Steer calves under 400 lbs were too lightly tested last week to develop an accurate market trend, however higher to sharply higher undertones were noticed on a higher quality offering. Steer calves 400-549 lbs sold mostly 10.00 higher, 550 lbs steers and heavier sold generally steady. Heifer calves under 450 lbs were too lightly tested last week to develop an accurate market trend, however higher undertones were noticed. 450-499 lbs heifer calves sold 10.00-20.00 higher, 500-649 lbs higher sold mostly 5.00-10.00 higher, heifers over 650 lbs were too lightly tested to develop any market trend. Calves were offered in mostly moderate size packages this week with a few light load lots seen. Quality this week was mixed but mostly average to attractive. Some calves showed signs of stress after an early week rain and snow storm. Many cutback calves continue to be seen off summer video sales. A wide variety of quality and breed types were seen again this sale. Demand for light weight calves did diminish as buyers filled loads leading to wide price on light weight offerings. Market activity was mostly active with a larger buyer pool noticed. Billings livestock commission will not sale cows or bulls again this fall on Thursdays. Cows will be sold on Mondays during the fall run. Supply included: 100% Feeder Cattle (65% Steers, 34% Heifers, 1% Bulls). Feeder cattle supply over 600 lbs was 21%.",
